    "body": "  - Introduces Tamagui as the app’s authoritative styling layer,\r\n  including shared tokens, themes, scale helpers, provider wiring, and\r\n  reusable primitives such as `AppText`, `Stack`, `Surface`,\r\n  `InputFrame`, and `PressableSurface`.\r\n  - Migrates shared components, navigation, dashboard, payment, QR,\r\n  history, mint, settings, restore, and modal surfaces away from legacy\r\n  `Txt`, `TxtInput`, `colors.ts`, and `react-native-size-matters`\r\n  styling.\r\n  - Preserves native React Native boundaries where they still provide\r\n  platform behavior, including camera, sheets, scroll/list containers,\r\n  gesture/animation pieces, and specialized text-input refs.\r\n  - Adds `TAMA_MIGRATION.md` to document the completed migration\r\n  surface, intentional native boundaries, verification status, and known\r\n  non-Tamagui typecheck noise.",
